.TH OXIGUITAR-CLI 1 "October 2026" "OxiGuitar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oxiguitar\-cli \- print, convert and engrave guitar tablature files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oxiguitar\-cli info
.RB [ \-\-bars ]
.IR file ...
.br
.B oxiguitar\-cli detect
.IR file ...
.br
.B oxiguitar\-cli convert
.I file
.I new\-file
.br
.B oxiguitar\-cli render
.I file
.RB [ \-\-png
.IR prefix ]
.RB [ \-\-pdf
.IR file ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.BI "oxiguitar\-cli events " file
.br
.B oxiguitar\-cli tools
.br
.B oxiguitar\-cli specimen
.RB [ \-\-png
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-pdf
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-scale
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-dark ]
.br
.B oxiguitar\-cli version
.br
.B oxiguitar\-cli help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oxiguitar\-cli
is the command\-line companion of
.BR oxiguitar (1).
It reads and writes files through the same format plugins, from the same plugin folders
(see
.BR oxiguitar (1)),
and never creates or changes anything there.
The package
.B oxiguitar\-plugins\-basic
holds the plugins for Guitar Pro files, versions 3 to 8.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR info " [" \-\-bars "] \fIfile\fR..."
Print the structure of each file: its format, header, bars, tracks and the
import log.
.B \-\-bars
adds a line per bar and track.
.TP
.BI detect " file" ...
Print the format of each file and the plugin that reads it, recognised from
its contents rather than its extension.
.TP
.BI convert " file new\-file"
Read
.I file
and write it as
.IR new\-file ,
in the format its extension names (.gp for Guitar Pro 7 and 8).
Prints what the new file can't hold (its losses), each with the first bar
and track it happens in, and notes on what Guitar Pro does differently.
.TP
.BI render " file"
Engrave a score to PNG pages and/or a PDF.
.TP
.BI events " file"
Print the score as it plays: the bars in playing order (repeats, endings,
D.C. and D.S., codas) with their times in seconds, every note with its
start, end, string, pitch, velocity and effects, and the metronome's clicks.
.TP
.B tools
List the tools, as in the Tools menu of
.BR oxiguitar (1).
.TP
.B specimen
Draw the renderer's test page into a PNG and/or a PDF.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of the commands.
.SH RENDER OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-png " prefix"
Write PNG pages
.IR prefix \-1.png,
.IR prefix \-2.png,
and so on.
Long sheets are cut into PNGs of at most 8192 pixels.
.TP
.BI \-\-pdf " file"
Write a PDF, always in pages.
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " n"
Pixels per point in the PNGs (default 2).
.TP
.B \-\-dark
Draw a dark page.
.TP
.BR \-\-layout " page|vertical|horizontal|parchment"
The staff layout (default page).
.TP
.BI \-\-width " pt"
The window width for the vertical layout.
.TP
.BR \-\-paper " a4|letter"
The paper size.
.TP
.BR \-\-tracks " \fIlist\fR|all"
The tracks to engrave, as numbers separated by commas (default: the first).
.TP
.BI \-\-staff\-space " pt"
The distance between staff lines.
.TP
.BI \-\-notation " track" = notation ,...
Each track's notation:
.BR std ", " tab " or " both
(default: tab for fretted instruments).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dynamics
Hide dynamics markings.
.TP
.BI \-\-tool " id"
Run a tool on the score first, as the Tools menu does; may be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Report only errors.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every file was read (and, for
.BR convert ,
written), 1 if any could not be, 2 on bad usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME " and " OXIGUITAR_HOME
choose the settings and the plugin folder, as for
.BR oxiguitar (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B oxiguitar\-cli info song.gp5
Print the structure of song.gp5.
.TP
.B oxiguitar\-cli convert song.gp5 song.gp
Write song.gp5 as a Guitar Pro 7 file, song.gp.
.TP
.B oxiguitar\-cli render song.gp \-\-pdf song.pdf \-\-tracks all
Engrave every track of song.gp into a PDF.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/mateusrdp/oxiguitar/issues
.UE .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR oxiguitar (1)
